# Divine Intervention's last ability triggers only if its controller removes the last intervention counter from it (its
# ruling): one removed by another player's effect doesn't trigger it, and it can't trigger ever after. Each player has one:
# Bot1's, down to one counter after Bot1's turn 3 upkeep, loses it on turn 4 to Bot2's Vampire Hexmage - the last counter,
# removed by the controller of that ability (CR 608.2c), Bot2 - and the game goes on: neither Bot1's Divine Intervention
# (Bot2 removed it) nor Bot2's (not its counter) triggers. Bot1's turn 5 upkeep ability finds no counter to remove (CR
# 122.1), and the game still goes on; Bot2's own Divine Intervention, which Bot2's turn 4 upkeep took to one counter, takes
# its last in Bot2's turn 6 upkeep, and that draws the game (CR 104.4c).

